note S5 scrub with OM-2 pinned global registers (pinset/pinlo): scrub clears X18..X26, then sets the
note pinned base of g and the pinned length of h (5000, above 4095) back, so the reads after it give the
note stored values. A lost base faults (139) and a lost length traps 3 (103); exit 0 is the pass.
om2
global g ulong 10
global h ulong 5000
fn main to int
j = ulong 4999
put h j 7
put g 9 5
k = scrub 64
y = get h j
if ne y 7
ret 2
end
if ne get g 9 5
ret 3
end
ret int k
end
